// expect: 42
// mn-mutual-negation-gate — a declaration over a MUTUALLY-RECURSIVE callee
// that declares `!Mutate` may itself declare a closed clause beside the
// negation. `outer` declares `Cast + !Mutate` and its body proves
// `Cast(Int) + !Mutate`; the gate holds and the program runs to 42.
//
// It refused once (Hβ.effects.negative-stance-under-mixed-gate): the least
// solution of a recursive row equation cut only at the declaration's OWN
// row, so a tail landing on a co-member's row never closed and the widened
// tail reached every caller's gate. The one-pass judgment closes every
// cycle at its binding group, and this fixture is that rule's standing
// witness. It rotted unregistered when `addr` began answering an address
// and its comparison became a type error; the cast is a statement now and
// the comparison reads the callee's number, and the frontier runs it.
import memory

fn ping(n) with !Mutate = if n <= 0 { 0 } else { pong(n - 1) }

fn pong(n) with !Mutate = if n <= 0 { 1 } else { ping(n - 1) }

fn outer(x) with Cast + !Mutate = {
  let _ = addr(x)
  ping(x)
}

fn main() = if outer(3) > 0 { 42 } else { 1 }
